{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfUSrsjE7GBTHXR5gjPA7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Do both, in parallel. The training path is cheap enough ($24K total) that it's a near-free hedge regardless of what happens with the hire — and it builds durable team depth that outlasts any one person, which matters given you already lost 2 of 7 to attrition last year. The real risk is relying on hiring alone: \"3 months\" is a search *estimate*, not a guarantee, and against a hard customer commitment you don't want your only path to competency to be a variable-timeline external search.\n\nThe main tradeoff is cost (~$219K combined vs. $195K or $24K alone) against timeline risk — but for a committed customer deliverable, that delta is probably small next to the cost of missing the date. One thing worth checking before committing: does the senior hire's onboarding compress the \"several more months\" of on-the-job ramp for the two mid-levels (e.g., by pairing them), since that's what actually determines whether you hit 6 months."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":40637,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d9a680d3-a98c-4d0b-9579-0b1f69333f48","uuid":"103c9b19-ebd5-4cfc-a885-af3f5971cdeb","timestamp":"2026-09-27T18:50:54.553Z","request_id":"req_011CfUSrsJRpT7XnFBcx5bFJ"}
